B.acQ=new A.dS('      A card\'s **Life** determines how many [[Damage Counter | damage counters]] a [[Creature | creature]] can sustain before\n      being destroyed. It is essentially the value of the creature maximum damage threshold.\n\n      It is important to note that creatures do not have a first-class concept of "current life". Each card on the\n      field has a fixed number of damage counters and their maximum life, which is just referred to as "Life". If a\n      creature receives a "+1 Life" bonus, the number of damage counters it has does not change (which means that their\n      effective "current life" increases).\n      ',!0)
